  "description": "AHUXAE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H96 Gd3 N9 Ni6 O33,5.75(C2 H3 N1),1.5(H2 O1),2(C4 H10 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Gd21? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd22? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd12? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd11? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd31? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Gd32? (Gd) has 0 O neighbors; Ni21? (Ni) has 0 O neighbors; Ni61? (Ni) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 9 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.841-3.741 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.05-108.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni6Gd3(OH)6(HL)6(NO3)3]·5.75MeCN·2Et2O·1.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
